1162: \]
1163: Thus its actual central source is the nodal quotient of the Tate
1164: chain, with the degree-zero line glued by \(c\). The kernel map
1165: (SZ.45) acts on that line, including the source automorphism
1166: on the normalization. It has not been replaced by the identity.
1167: 
1168: One can verify a uniform contraction on this retained line near
1169: the strict \(q_2\) face. Restrict to
1170: \(|q_2|\leq\eta|q_1|\), with fixed sufficiently small \(\eta\).
1171: Then \(|v|\) is comparable with \(|q_1|\).
1172: Use the usual Tate fundamental annulus
1173: \(|Q|\leq|Z|\leq1\), and interpolate a positive line metric
1174: between its two end values, whose ratio is \(|c|\).
1175: Its maximum-to-minimum ratio is at most
1176: \(C|q_1|^{-a}\). The same interpolation on the plumbing annuli
1177: extends to the nodal normalization, with its prescribed gluing
1178: at the two preimages of the node.
1179: 
1180: The source multiplier in (SZ.45) has magnitude bounded by
1181: \(C|q_1|^{-b}\), whereas \(|Q|\leq C|q_1|^2\).
1182: For sufficiently small \(|q_1|\), reindexing its image into the
1183: fundamental annulus uses at most two source periods when
1184: \((a,b)=(1,2)\), and at most one when \((a,b)=(2,1)\).
1185: Each reindexing contributes at most \(C|q_1|^{-a}\)
1186: to the line norm ratio. Formula (SZ.45) consequently gives the
1187: operator bounds
1188: \[
1189:  \|k\|\leq
1190:  \begin{cases}
1191:  C|\lambda_0|\,|q_1|^{N-4},&(a,b)=(1,2),\\
1192:  C|\lambda_0|\,|q_1|^{N-5},&(a,b)=(2,1).
1193:  \end{cases}                                                   \tag{SZ.46}
1194: \]
1195: For \(N\ge6\) these are strict contractions after shrinking.
1196: On compact subsets away from the exceptional intersection,
1197: the same conclusion follows by decreasing \(|\lambda_0|\).
1198: The norm shell therefore proves freeness and proper
1199: discontinuity of the retained kernel period on its nonzero
1200: line. At \(q_2=0\) this is a statement on the actual normalized
1201: nodal line with its node gluing, not on a substitute product.
1202: 
1203: At the strict \(v=0\) face the kernel of \(E\) is generated by
1204: the source period \(h\). Its transverse character is \(Z\),
1205: and its exact multiplier is \(Q=q_1q_2u_Q\). On that face,
1206: away from the collision, \(q_1=q_2=T\) and
1207: \(0<|Q|<1\) on a small source tube. Hence this residual action
1208: is the actual Tate contraction in \(Z\). Its other component,
1209: the line multiplier \(P^a\), is retained on the component
1210: chain. These two kernel actions supply the required proper
1211: rank-one face quotients. The common-face subdivisions and
1212: their collision quotient are still separate geometric work.
